# Partial-catch guard (error-model.md §11 Increment 2 (C)): a Div has TWO fault
# categories, and catching ONLY one does NOT swallow the other. Here the catch
# names Fault.DivByZero, but the fault is `INT_MIN / -1` (an OVERFLOW), so it is
# UNCAUGHT and PANICS `integer overflow` — uniformly on both backends (the GIR
# emits the panic, so the LIR only ever branches; no backend-specific UB).
void main():
    int imin = -9223372036854775807 - 1
    int neg1 = -1
    int r = (imin / neg1) catch Fault.DivByZero: 0
    print(f"{r}")
